  {
    "id": "eclipse-score/communication#1261",
    "patches": [
      {
        "path": "contributions/issues/eclipse-score/communication/1261/communication-1261.patch",
        "registry_path_exists": true,
        "sha256": "be96156d1e937865f180444117f9ba4285de08862c28971d0ab445eb45a36698",
        "sha_matches": true,
        "mail_header": "From 4760fe47f2edc25c16f7f76f70c68397feb90586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: jnsagai <jnsagai@gmail.com>\nDate: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:54:16 +0100\nSubject: [PATCH] Rust::com: Add async stream of newly available services\n\nAddresses #1261.\n\nAdd Runtime::find_all_services(), an asynchronous stream of\ninterface-independent ServiceDescriptor items (service type name, version,\nbinding, binding service id and instance id).\n\nThe LoLa backend starts one find-any watch per service type present in the\nloaded configuration (including add-on configurations merged before the\nstream is opened) and reports any concrete provider instance id. Services\nthat are already offered are yielded first; an identity is yielded again\nwhen it is re-offered after a withdrawal. Pending items are coalesced: at\nmost one item per currently offered identity, discarded if the service is\nwithdrawn before being polled, which bounds the backlog by the offered set.\nThe stream ends when it is dropped, which stops every native watch.\nDiscovery callbacks only hold a weak reference to the stream state.\n\nIRuntime gains GetConfiguredServiceWildcardIdentifiers(), declared last\nwith a default implementation. Runtime serializes add-on configuration\nmerges with the wildcard enumeration and invalidates its cache; returned\nidentifiers stay valid in address-stable storage.\n\nAdds LoLa backend unit tests and the all_services_stream ITF integration\ntest (initial offer, later offer, withdrawal, re-offer with exact\nidentities and duplicate detection).\n\nImplemented with DeepSeek V4 Flash (Fabro) and corrected by Claude.\nOpen design points (configured-service scope, operational-phase\nallocation) are raised on #1261.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n---\n score/mw/com/impl/i_runtime.h                 |  17 +\n score/mw/com/impl/runtime.cpp                 |  76 +++\n score/mw/com/impl/runtime.h                   |  25 +\n .../com-api/com-api-ffi-lola